 "text": "Property & Taxes | Daviess County, IN\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nGovernment\nServices\nAbout Us\nCommunity\nSearch\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments\nAuditor's Office\nProperty & Taxes\nProperty & Taxes\nAll property transfers are required to be recorded in the county Recorder's Office before they will be transferred on the plat books and property tax rolls. A sales disclosure form (if applicable) along with a sales disclosure form fee of $10 (if applicable) is required in the Auditor's Office along with the transfer document.\nAll delinquent property taxes and special assessments must be paid before parcels and be combined or split.\nFor more information on Property & Tax information, you may contact the Treasurer's Office and/or the Auditor's Office .\n9\n1\n1\n2\nDeductions\nSee the Indiana Department of Local Government Finance website for information about property tax deductions.\nTax Rate Chart (PDF)\nView the County's Tax Rate Chart (PDF).\nTaxing Units\nSee a list of Taxing Units in Daviess County.\nDeductions\nTax Rate Chart (PDF)\nTaxing Units\nAgendas & Minutes\nNotify Me®\nSheriff's\nDepartment\nParcel Search\nPay Property\nTaxes Online\nMeetings\non Youtube\n-->\nDaviess County Indiana\nCourthouse - 200 E. Walnut St.\nGovernment Center - 300 E. Hefron St.\nWashington, IN 47501\nHome\nSite Map\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×",
